<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech Nov retail sales rise 8.3 percent yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Czech Nov retail sales rise 8.3 percent yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Czech November retail sales, in real terms, rose 8.3 percent compared with the same month in 1995, the Czech Statistical Bureau (CSU) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The CSU also said that total internal trade rose by 9.2 percent year-on-year in real terms in November.  </p>
<p> CZECH REAL RETAIL SALES	 NOV 96   OCT  96   JAN-NOV 96</p>
<p>  pct change yr/yr		 +8.3    +14.7	 +9.2</p>
<p>CZECH REAL INTERNAL TRADE</p>
<p>  pct change yr/yr		 +9.2    +14.2	+11.4</p>
<p>Note: All figures are preliminary. Total internal trade includes retail sales plus sales and repairs of motor cars, motor fuel, restaurant services and accommodation.  </p>
<p>The CSU also gave the following real retail sales data (percentage change year- on-year):</p>
<p>				     NOV 96   OCT 96  JAN-NOV 96</p>
<p>sales, repairs of motor</p>
<p> vehicles plus motor fuel     12.7	16.1     23.3</p>
<p>restaurants and</p>
<p> accommodation		     8.4	 6.1	7.1</p>
<p>TRANSPORT</p>
<p>  total			     -4.0	 5.7     11.9</p>
<p>  railways			 -11.5	10.7	2.4</p>
<p>  road transport		  -3.0	-2.4	8.5</p>
<p>  river			    -43.7	37.1    -24.8</p>
<p>  air				-22.6     -19.5     -4.7</p>
<p>parallel and support   activities</p>
<p>					16.6	26.8     31.5</p>
<p>-- Robin Shepherd, Prague Newsroom 42-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
